Package: panelviz
Type: Package
Title: Import, Aggregate and Visualise Any Panel Data
Version: 0.0.1
Authors@R: person(given = "Carlos", family = "Morales", role = c("aut", "cre"), email = "moralec@gmail.com")
Description: Visualise any panel data (also called longitudinal data, repeated
    measures or time-series cross-section: the same individuals observed over time).
    Declare which column is the individual and which is time; the id and time
    formats are recognised (dates, years, quarters, months, ISO weeks, Stata date
    formats, plain indices), the data is aggregated in two stages (within individual
    over time, then across individuals by group), and publication-quality charts are
    drawn. Generalises the plotting approach of 'wpa' and 'vivainsights'.
URL: https://github.com/moralec/panelviz
BugReports: https://github.com/moralec/panelviz/issues
License: MIT + file LICENSE
Encoding: UTF-8
Roxygen: list(markdown = TRUE)
Depends: R (>= 4.1.0)
Imports: cli, dplyr, ggplot2, grid, rlang, scales, tibble, tidyr, tidyselect
Suggests: haven, ragg, readr, systemfonts, testthat (>= 3.0.0)
Config/testthat/edition: 3
